{"id":"banano","es":"banano","en":["banana"],"pos":"noun","topic":"food","note":"m. The Colombian word for the sweet one you peel and eat.","sent":{"es":"Me comí un {banano} en el desayuno.","en":"I had a banana for breakfast."}}
{"id":"arepa","es":"arepa","en":["arepa"],"pos":"noun","topic":"food","note":"f. The maize flatbread at the heart of Colombian breakfast.","sent":{"es":"Desayuno {arepa} con huevo.","en":"I have an arepa with egg for breakfast."}}
{"id":"frijoles","es":"frijoles","en":["beans"],"pos":"noun","topic":"food","note":"m. pl. The base of a bandeja paisa.","sent":{"es":"La bandeja paisa lleva {frijoles}.","en":"A bandeja paisa comes with beans."}}
{"id":"maiz","es":"maíz","en":["sweetcorn","maize"],"pos":"noun","topic":"food","note":"m. Arepas are made from it.","sent":{"es":"La arepa es de {maíz}.","en":"The arepa is made of maize."}}
{"id":"naranja","es":"naranja","en":["orange"],"pos":"noun","topic":"food","note":"f. The fruit. Fresh juice is jugo de naranja.","sent":{"es":"Un jugo de {naranja}, por favor.","en":"An orange juice, please."}}
