{"id":"dulce","es":"dulce","en":["sweet"],"pos":"adjective","topic":"food","note":"As a noun, un dulce is a sweet.","sent":{"es":"Este café está muy {dulce}.","en":"This coffee is very sweet."}}
{"id":"salado","es":"salado","en":["salty"],"pos":"adjective","topic":"food","note":"In Colombia also unlucky: ¡qué salado!","sent":{"es":"La sopa está muy {salada}.","en":"The soup is very salty."}}
{"id":"picante","es":"picante","en":["spicy"],"pos":"adjective","topic":"food","note":"Colombian food is mild; ají, the hot sauce, is served on the side.","sent":{"es":"¿Esto es {picante}?","en":"Is this spicy?"}}
{"id":"hielo","es":"hielo","en":["ice"],"pos":"noun","topic":"food","note":"m.","sent":{"es":"Una limonada sin {hielo}.","en":"A lemonade without ice."}}
{"id":"aceite","es":"aceite","en":["oil"],"pos":"noun","topic":"food","note":"m.","sent":{"es":"Fríelo en un poco de {aceite}.","en":"Fry it in a little oil."}}
